{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,10]],"date-time":"2026-09-10T17:05:38Z","timestamp":1789059938735,"version":"build-2803163510"},"reference-count":60,"publisher":"Optica Publishing Group","issue":"11","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,19]],"date-time":"2025-05-19T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1747612800000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1364\/OA_License_v2#VOR-OA"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,19]],"date-time":"2025-05-19T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1747612800000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/opg.optica.org\/policies\/opg-tdm-policy.json"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001348","name":"Agency for Science, Technology and Research","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["NRF 2021-QEP2-02-P12"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["NRF 2021-QEP2-02-P12"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001348","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001381","name":"National Research Foundation Singapore","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["NRF CRP24-2020-0003"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["NRF CRP24-2020-0003"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001381","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["opg.optica.org"],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Opt. Express"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,6,2]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>An Ising machine stands as a compelling solution for large-scale combinatorial optimization problems, leveraging its unconventional computational architecture. We propose an optical parallel feedback system, employing mutual injection locking of vertical-cavity surface-emitting lasers (VCSELs) and programmable spatial light modulators (SLMs), specifically aimed at removing electrical bottlenecks to achieve all-optical computation. Through simulation results, the ability to solve a 16-bit square-lattice MAXCUT optimization problem is analyzed. As a proof-of-concept, we demonstrate an optical injection lock using single-mode master and slave VCSELs. Remarkably, we achieve polarization switching with less than 1% of the master VCSEL\u2019s injection power. Building upon this modest achievement, we outline a roadmap envisioning the integration of advanced nanophotonic devices, particularly metasurface-enabled SLMs and VCSELs. This strategic evolution targets scalability and programmability while upholding an all-optical computing paradigm.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1364\/oe.546402","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,12,13]],"date-time":"2024-12-13T07:00:13Z","timestamp":1734073213000},"page":"22119","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1364\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":9,"title":["All-optical scalable and programmable VCSEL-based Ising annealer with parallel feedback"],"prefix":"10.1364","volume":"33","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0005-5426-5869","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Dewen","family":"Zhang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/01tgyzw49","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Zifeng","family":"Yuan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/01tgyzw49","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-6815-487X","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Thanh Xuan","family":"Hoang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Technology and Research (A\u2605STAR)"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Wujie","family":"Fu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/01tgyzw49","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Ching Eng","family":"Png","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Techn